{
  "dom_id": "step-q101923",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The value $z=0$ satisfies which of the following inequalities?\n\nI. $z+3\\ge 1$\n\nII. $3z+1<0$\n\nIII. $-6\\le \\frac{z}{2}-1\\le -2$",
  "worked_solution": "We substitute the given value into each of the inequalities and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $z=0$ into the first inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+3 & \\ge 1 \\\\ 0+3 & \\ge 1 \\\\ 3 & \\ge 1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $z=0$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $z=0$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $z=0$ into the second inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z+1 & <0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 0+1 & <0 \\\\ 1 & <0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $z=0$ leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $z=0$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $z=0$ into the third inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6\\le \\frac{z}{2}-1 & \\le -2 \\\\ -6\\le \\frac{0}{2}-1 & \\le -2 \\\\ -6\\le -1 & \\le -2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $z=0$ leads to a **false** statement.  \n\nTherefore, $z=0$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
